<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cultural patronage</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cultural patronage is the sponsorship of art, architecture, literature and learning by rulers and elites. It was a recurring means by which empires displayed legitimacy, attracted talent and left lasting legacies. Examples include the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wisdom">House of Wisdom</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>, the architecture and miniatures of the Timurid and Safavid empires, the monuments of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> and the scholarship of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-renaissance">Carolingian Renaissance</a>.</p></div>
